{"kind":"article","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMA","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMAOrder","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMACriterion"],"title":"Automated Time Series","anchor":"Automated-Time-Series"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Concurrent Order Selection with AutoARIMA","role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection","modules":[{"name":"SwiftForecast"}]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMAParallel","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Manually diagnosing autocorrelation functions (ACF) and partial autocorrelation functions (PACF) to select ARIMA orders is time-consuming and error-prone. Standard automated packages like R’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"forecast::auto.arima","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or Python’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"pmdarima","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" search across candidate orders sequentially.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"AutoARIMA","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" evaluates the entire hyperparameter lattice simultaneously across all CPU cores on Apple Silicon using structured Swift Concurrency (","type":"text"},{"code":"withThrowingTaskGroup","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Grid Search Architecture","anchor":"Grid-Search-Architecture","type":"heading"},{"code":["           Observed Time Series [y_1, y_2, ..., y_N]","                               │","       ┌───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┐","       ▼                       ▼                       ▼","ARIMA(1, 1, 0)          ARIMA(2, 1, 1)          ARIMA(0, 1, 2)","Task 1                  Task 2                  Task 3","   │                       │                       │","   ├─ Hannan-Rissanen      ├─ Hannan-Rissanen      ├─ Hannan-Rissanen","   └─ Compute AIC\/BIC      └─ Compute AIC\/BIC      └─ Compute AIC\/BIC","       │                       │                       │","       └───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┘","                               ▼","                withThrowingTaskGroup Collector","                               │","                               ▼","                 Sorted Leaderboard & Best Model"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"Information Criteria","anchor":"Information-Criteria","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"AIC (Akaike Information Criterion)"}]},{"text":": Penalizes model complexity while rewarding likelihood:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"$$\\text{AIC} = 2k - 2\\ln(L)$$","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"BIC (Bayesian Information Criterion)"}]},{"text":": Imposes a stronger penalty proportional to sample size:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"$$\\text{BIC} = k\\ln(N) - 2\\ln(L)$$","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":2,"text":"Example Usage","anchor":"Example-Usage","type":"heading"},{"code":["import SwiftForecast","","\/\/ 1. Initialize AutoARIMA with bounded search ranges","let autoArima = AutoARIMA(","    maxP: 3,","    maxD: 2,","    maxQ: 3,","    criterion: .aic",")","","\/\/ 2. Concurrently fit candidates across all cores","let result = try await autoArima.fit(series: historicalPrices)","print(\"Optimal Order: \\(autoArima.bestOrder!) with AIC: \\(autoArima.bestScore!)\")","","\/\/ 3. Generate multi-step forecasts","let forecast = try await autoArima.forecast(horizon: 12)","print(\"Forecasted points: \\(forecast.forecast.predictions)\")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"Stability & Convergence Guarantees","anchor":"Stability--Convergence-Guarantees","type":"heading"},{"level":3,"text":"Zero-Variance Degenerate Inputs","anchor":"Zero-Variance-Degenerate-Inputs","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If an input series is constant or exhibits zero numerical variance ($\\text{var} < 10^{-12}$), standard likelihood optimization can diverge or enter infinite loops. ","type":"text"},{"code":"AutoARIMA","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" detects zero variance upfront, immediately fitting an exact ARIMA(0, 0, 0) constant model:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Avoids matrix singularities in the Hannan-Rissanen and Yule-Walker algorithms.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Guarantees instant return without stalling the task group.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":3,"text":"Fixed Iteration Bound","anchor":"Fixed-Iteration-Bound","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"All internal parameter search loops are strictly bounded by a ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations = 500","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ceiling, ensuring that optimization cannot exceed the configured iteration bound in deterministic time across parallel worker threads.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/autoarimaparallel"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/ArimaAndSarima","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/SmoothingAndDecomposition","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/KoopmanOperator"],"title":"Guides & Tutorials","anchor":"Guides--Tutorials"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Discover optimal autoregressive, integrated, and moving average orders across ((p, d, q) \\times (P, D, Q)_s) grids using parallel Swift Concurrency.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/KoopmanOperator":{"abstract":[{"text":"Koopman Operator time-series forecasting and dynamical system modeling actor.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Uses Extended Dynamic Mode Decomposition (EDMD) to approximate non-linear dynamics","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"via linear operators in lifted observable feature spaces.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"KoopmanOperator","url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/koopmanoperator","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"KoopmanOperator"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"KoopmanOperator"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/KoopmanOperator","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/AutoARIMAOrder":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/autoarimaorder","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMAOrder","role":"symbol","title":"AutoARIMAOrder","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A structure identifying the selected ARIMA \/ SARIMA order."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AutoARIMAOrder","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AutoARIMAOrder","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/ArimaAndSarima":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/arimaandsarima","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/ArimaAndSarima","abstract":[{"text":"Forecast univariate time series using Autoregressive Integrated Moving Average (ARIMA) and Seasonal ARIMA (SARIMA).","type":"text"}],"title":"ARIMA & SARIMA Time Series Models","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast","abstract":[{"text":"Time Series & Volatility Forecasting Models.","type":"text"}],"title":"SwiftForecast","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/SmoothingAndDecomposition":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/smoothinganddecomposition","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/SmoothingAndDecomposition","abstract":[{"text":"Model trends, seasonality, volatility, and dynamic state transitions using ","type":"text"},{"code":"ExponentialSmoothing","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"NelderMead","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"KalmanFilter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"GARCHModel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"TimeSeriesDecomposition","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"Time Series Forecasting, Smoothing & Kalman Filtering","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/AutoARIMACriterion":{"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AutoARIMACriterion"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AutoARIMACriterion"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMACriterion","url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/autoarimacriterion","title":"AutoARIMACriterion","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Information criterion utilized for model selection in "},{"code":"AutoARIMA","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/AutoARIMA":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/autoarima","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMA","role":"symb